@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}


<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

    <head>
        <title>About</title>

        <!--Page-specific styles-->
        <style>

            #top {
                margin-bottom: 40px;
            }

            #app {
                margin-top: 60px;
            }

            h3 {
            border-bottom: 1px solid #2E557C;
            }

        </style>

    </head>


    <body>
        <div id="top">
            <h1>About</h1>
            <i>Learn more about the application and the developer</i>
        </div>  

        <div id="app">
            <h3>The Application</h3>
            <p>
                The Lightsaber-Builder was made on the basis of allowing users to create their own lightsaber from
                the popular <i>Star Wars</i> Universe. 

                Users will be allowed to pick from the models of components that are used at Walt Disney World's Galaxy's Edge,
                where custom lightsabers can be made.

                
                Users can have part of this experience through this application using the styles of lightsaber components from the exhibit.

            </p>
        </div>

        <br />
        <br />

        <div id="credits">

            <h3>
                Credits
            </h3>


            <p>
                The models used for the lightsaber components are not owned by the developer. These 3D files (STL)
                were created by a user on the popular 3D-printing website "Thingiverse" and you can view them using
                the link below. These models are free use and will not be used for monetary purposes.
            <a href="https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:4159433">Lightsaber Models</a>
            
            </p>
        </div>
        <br />
        <br />

        <div id="dev">

            <h3>
                The Developer
            </h3>

            <p>
                I love Star Wars, I love to code. That's about all there is to it.
            </p>

        </div>

    </body>


</html>